---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import SectionHeading from "../../components/SectionHeading.astro";

const effectiveDate = "September 22, 2026";
const email = "christopherpombo4@gmail.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Simply Spend — Privacy Policy — Christopher Pombo"
  description="Privacy policy for Simply Spend: Expense Tracker. The app stores everything on your device, collects nothing, and has no servers, accounts, analytics, ads, or tracking."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Simply Spend — Privacy Policy"
    subtitle={`For Simply Spend: Expense Tracker. Effective ${effectiveDate}.`}
  />

  <article class="policy">
    <p class="policy__lede">
      Simply Spend keeps everything you enter on your own iPhone. I don't collect it, I can't see
      it, and there are no servers involved — the app has no way to send your information anywhere.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="What the app stores" />
    <p>
      Everything you type into Simply Spend — transaction names, amounts, dates, notes, categories,
      payment methods, and your app settings — is saved on your device, in the app's own storage. It
      stays there until you delete it or delete the app.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="What I collect" />
    <p>
      Nothing. There are no accounts to create, no sign-ins, and no way to use the app over the
      internet. Simply Spend contains no analytics, no crash reporting, no advertising, and no
      tracking of any kind. It includes no third-party software development kits, so no other
      company receives anything about you or your spending either.
    </p>
    <p>
      I have no servers and no database. Even if I wanted your financial information, the app is not
      built to send it to me.
    </p>
    <p>
      One exception worth naming, because it comes from iOS rather than from the app: if you've turned
      on <strong>Share With App Developers</strong> in Settings &rsaquo; Privacy &amp; Security &rsaquo;
      Analytics &amp; Improvements, Apple may share anonymous crash reports and general usage
      statistics with me. Those come from Apple under <a
        href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's privacy policy</a
      >, and they never include your transactions or anything you enter in the app.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Permissions" />
    <p>
      Simply Spend asks for no permissions. It does not use your camera, photos, microphone,
      location, contacts, or Face ID, and it does not send notifications.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Exporting your own data" />
    <p>
      The app can export your transactions as a CSV file, from Settings. When you do that, iOS asks
      where to send it — Files, Mail, AirDrop, or another app you choose. That file goes wherever you
      send it, and I never receive a copy. Once it leaves Simply Spend, it's covered by the privacy
      policy of whatever app or service you sent it to.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Backups" />
    <p>
      If you back up your iPhone to iCloud or to a computer, that backup may include Simply Spend's
      data, the same as any other app. Those backups are made and handled by Apple under{" "}
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Apple's privacy policy</a
      >. I have no access to them.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Deleting your data" />
    <p>
      Settings has an "Erase All Data" option that removes all your financial data — transactions,
      categories, payment methods, and budget settings. Your app preferences, like the theme and
      haptics switches, are left as you set them. Deleting the app from your iPhone removes
      everything, preferences included. Because nothing is stored anywhere else, there's nothing for
      me to delete on your behalf and no request you need to send me.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Children" />
    <p>
      Simply Spend is not directed at children under 13, and I don't knowingly collect information
      from anyone — including children — because the app collects nothing at all.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Changes to this policy" />
    <p>
      If the app ever changes in a way that affects your privacy, I'll update this page and change
      the effective date at the top before that version reaches the App Store. It's worth checking
      back here after an update if you want to be sure.
    </p>

    <SectionHeading text="Contact" />
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or the app are welcome: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="policy__meta">Developer: Christopher Pombo · Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .policy__lede {
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .policy :global(.section-heading) {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .policy__meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: var(--font-size-small);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
